# Exact Claude Code CLI pin for backlog-burn.yml and design-run.yml
# (issue #875 / Cipher rulings on #876). Both workflows read this file in
# trusted preflight: GPG-verify the release manifest, sha256-check the
# linux-x64 binary against the signed manifest AND the pin below, then
# install root-owned under /opt/claude-code/<ver>/claude.
#
# How to bump:
#   1. Change `version:` to the new exact X.Y.Z (never "latest").
#   2. Fetch https://downloads.claude.ai/claude-code-releases/<ver>/manifest.json
#      (+ .sig), gpg --verify with the fingerprint below, and copy
#      platforms.linux-x64.checksum into `linux-x64-sha256:`.
#   3. Confirm anthropics/claude-code-action still matches or keep
#      path_to_claude_code_executable authoritative.
#   4. Keep CLAUDE_CODE_SUBPROCESS_ENV_SCRUB=1; do not set SCRUB=0.
#   5. Do NOT add kernel.apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns=0 — use the
#      bwrap-userns-restrict AppArmor profile instead (Cipher on #876).
#
# Supply chain: claude.ai/install.sh is NOT used. The vendor HTTPS manifest
# is GPG-signed; we import the key, require this fingerprint, gpg --verify
# the .sig, then check the binary digest against both the signed manifest
# and linux-x64-sha256 below.
